    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0408" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg398"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 629.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 24, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In connexion with my despatches, No. 610,
                    of the 10th, and No. 623, of the 18th instant, both of them growing out of the
                    instructions contained in <pb facs="0409" n="399" xml:id="pg399"/> your No. 847,
                    of the 17th of February, I now transmit a copy of Lord Russell’s note of the
                    19th instant in reply.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d152-a1.xml" xpointer="d152-a1"/>
            </div>
